{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Emanuelle Goes to Dinosaur Land" is the of the fourth season of the American television comedy series "30 Rock", and the 79th overall episode of the series.","title":"Emanuelle Goes to Dinosaur Land"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was written by supervising producer Matt Hubbard and directed by Beth McCarthy-Miller.","title":"Emanuelle Goes to Dinosaur Land"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The episode originally aired on the National Broadcasting Company (NBC) network in the United States on May 13, 2010.","title":"Emanuelle Goes to Dinosaur Land"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Guest stars in this episode include John Anderson, Elizabeth Banks, Jon Hamm, Kristin McGee, Julianne Moore, Michael Sheen, Jason Sudeikis, and Dean Winters.","title":"Emanuelle Goes to Dinosaur Land"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Michael C. Flessas (born June 2, 1959 in Miami, Florida), is the birth name of American actor Michael Flessas, who is of Greek ancestry.","title":"Michael Flessas"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Flessas' most notable film role was "Angry Man" in the Cannes Film Festival 2000 Palme d'Or winning film "Dancer in the Dark" directed by Danish film director Lars von Trier.","title":"Michael Flessas"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Originally, the director himself considered playing the role but, instead, the role was given to Flessas.","title":"Michael Flessas"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" "Dancer in the Dark" starred Icelandic singer/actress Björk who won the Best Actress award at Cannes for her role.","title":"Michael Flessas"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" French film icon, César Award winner, and Academy Award nominee Catherine Deneuve, and other noteworthy artists such as Academy Award and Tony Award winner Joel Grey, Peter Stormare, David Morse, and Stellan Skarsgård also performed in the multiple prize winning film.","title":"Michael Flessas"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" One of Björk's songs for the film received an Academy Award nomination for Best Song.","title":"Michael Flessas"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mathilde Bonnefoy (born 11 March 1972) is a French film editor and director who was nominated for an ACE Eddie Award for the editing of the film "Run Lola Run" (1998) and who won the award for editing the documentary "Citizenfour" (2014).","title":"Mathilde Bonnefoy"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She and her husband Dirk Wilutzky additionally served as producers of "Citizenfour" with its director Laura Poitras, and the three received the 2014 Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature.","title":"Mathilde Bonnefoy"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 5th Africa Movie Academy Awards ceremony was held on April 4, 2009 at the Gloryland Cultural Center in Yenagoa, Bayelsa State, Nigeria, to honor the best African films of 2008.","title":"5th Africa Movie Academy Awards"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was broadcast live on Nigerian national television.","title":"5th Africa Movie Academy Awards"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Africa Movie Academy Award winner Kate Henshaw-Nuttal and Nigerian stand-up comedian Julius Agwu hosted the ceremony.","title":"5th Africa Movie Academy Awards"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Numerous celebrities graced the event, including Timipre Sylva (the Governor of Bayelsa State) and Nollywood actresses and actors.","title":"5th Africa Movie Academy Awards"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Special guests were Academy Award winner Forest Whitaker and Hollywood actor Danny Glover.","title":"5th Africa Movie Academy Awards"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Roger Ross Williams (born September 16, 1973) is an American television news, documentary and entertainment director, producer and writer.","title":"Roger Ross Williams"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He directed most notably "Music by Prudence" that won the Academy Award for Best Documentary (Short Subject), about a 21-year-old Zimbabwean singer-songwriter Prudence Mabhena, who was born severely disabled and has struggled to overcome poverty and discrimination.","title":"Roger Ross Williams"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" All other seven members of Prudence's band "Liyana" are also disabled.","title":"Roger Ross Williams"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Williams's film "God Loves Uganda", which premiered at the 2013 Sundance Film Festival to enormous critical acclaim.","title":"Roger Ross Williams"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It was shortlisted for a 2014 Academy Award, has won over a dozen awards and screened at over 60 film festivals worldwide.","title":"Roger Ross Williams"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" His latest film "Life, Animated" was nominated for the 2017 Academy Award.","title":"Roger Ross Williams"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Killer Films is a New York City-based independent film production company founded by movie producers Christine Vachon and Pamela Koffler in 1995.","title":"Killer Films"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The company has produced a number of the most acclaimed American independent films over the past two decades including "Far From Heaven" (nominated for four Academy Awards), "Boys Don't Cry" (Academy Award winner), "One Hour Photo", "Kids", "Hedwig and the Angry Inch", "Happiness", "Velvet Goldmine", "Safe", "I Shot Andy Warhol", "Swoon", "I'm Not There" (Academy Award nominated), "Kill Your Darlings", "Still Alice" (Academy Award winner) and "Carol" (nominated for six Academy Awards).","title":"Killer Films"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Killer Films executive produced Todd Haynes' five episode HBO miniseries "Mildred Pierce" featuring Kate Winslet and Guy Pearce, which went on to win five Emmys, a Golden Globe and a Screen Actors Guild Award.","title":"Killer Films"}],"peer_messages":["3,"text":" Numerous celebrities graced the event, including Timipre Sylva (the Governor of Bayelsa State) and Nollywood actresses and actors.","title":"5th Africa Movie Academy Awards"}
